 "method": "Figs. 2-4 of arXiv:2502.08563v1 are embedded raster images (no vector paths), extracted with PyMuPDF and digitised from pixels. Fig. 3 (page 7, 500x324 px): axes calibrated from the frame and grey grid lines (0.02 W per 58.1 px, 2 kHz per 38.8 px; 1 px = 0.00034 W x 0.052 kHz); each coloured branch is the column-wise median of its colour mask, so the model line and the data markers lying on it are merged (where markers sit off the line, e.g. the red branch below 0.245 W, the median lies between them: about +-0.15 kHz). Fig. 4a (page 8, 556x639 px): axes from the inward tick marks (0.02 W per 101.3 px, 5 kHz per 71.5 px); the 25 power steps are the 3.5 mW-wide blocks between intensity discontinuities; peaks are maxima (prominence >= 60 in summed RGB, parabolic sub-pixel) of the block-averaged column profile, with the white arrows masked. Some peaks are noise or arrow residue (e.g. 126.77 kHz at 0.3364 W). Fig. 4b dark points: the powers where the upper ridge has no resolvable peak.",
